    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0213" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg79"/>

                <head>No. 68.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 7,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 505.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your telegram of the 30th
                    ultimo, saying that the Nicaraguan Congress had rejected the boundary convention
                    with Costa Rica.</p>
                <pb facs="0214" n="80" xml:id="pg80"/>
                <p>Similar information had already been received here through the diplomatic
                    representatives of those Governments at this capital; and in a note to the Costa
                    Rican minister, after acknowledging his upon that subject, I have said, “that I
                    thus learn with regret that the expected course of direct settlement of the
                    questions between two countries to which the United States are equally friendly
                    is interrupted.”</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
